Z||000005||fieroshop||04-15-2000||01:27 AM||||Hey guys, I've tried just about every plug in the Fiero and finally found out that all thos expensive plugs are no better for hp gains or gas gains. So I use the oem plugs Delco and have had no problem with any Fiero That I have to tune up in my shop. If you want to spend alot of money. Go ahead and buy the expensive plugs. I mean it is your money and not mine.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fiasco||04-15-2000||01:34 AM||||No, see, I wanted someone else to buy the 'spensive suckers and let me know that they're no better... no need now though- <BR>I guess you've done that. -Thanks for the info.||||reg||1
Z||000007||TheFiero64||04-15-2000||09:52 AM||||Don't use autolite! I have never had a set that lasts. The always misfire or foul up in everything that I've tried them in.||||reg||1
Z||000008||TooLowFiero||04-15-2000||10:32 AM||||i am using the bosch +4's in my 86 2.5 liter and i think they are great (i worked for an aouto biz and only paid 5.99 for all 4 shhhhh) i did notice improved starting and about a mile a gallon more gas wise.<BR>well just my $.02<P>TooLow||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||04-15-2000||03:08 PM||||According to reports I have the 87+ DIS motors do not like Bosch Platinum plugs, either type. If you use these please post wether or not they last and how long. ((If they last more than a month they are OK. My informations says they likely won't last 2 weeks.)) <P>If the bosch plugs fail I would like to see them. IF you want to return them as defective I can mail them back after I look at them. I really need to see a dead set of them.||||reg||1
Z||000010||RobertVol||04-16-2000||11:44 PM||||Actually I have used and still use Rapid fires in my car and they are running better than the stock plugs. I have seen better or should I say " smoother" acceleration out of my car.Sometimes...... the time it takes to get to a certain speed is not as nice as how much effort it takes. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||bHooper||04-17-2000||11:54 AM||||i have heard that the +4 may actually be bad for your car.  a friend who races SCCA says that those who have used them, have had a problem with them scortching and burning a hole in the piston.  apparently they are "too efficiant".<P>just reporting what i have heard, so do not base this on fact<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||HF6582||04-17-2000||12:30 PM||||While talking to the parts person at a parts store, he said that the +4's are usually one heat range higher than stock plugs.<BR> <BR>I have tried AC Delco rapid fires, and I think they don't even make a good paperweight.  The ground of the plug started to seperate. This was after about 4000 miles.<P>Currently I am running the +4's with good luck. Better accel and the idle is more stabile.<P>This is in a 2.8L.<P>In my 84, I run just the bosch platinums and it seems to run a little better.<P>Scott <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
